%% DM26-0670

%% A client reconnects after its connection dropped, as built (2026-10-21, docs/architecture/cassini-broker.md and
%% cassini-client-reliability.md), with the identity check that is designed (policy-enforcement.md, stage 0).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Agent (TcpClientActor)
    participant Listener as new Listener
    participant SM as SessionManager
    participant SA as SessionAgent (detached)

    Note over Client,SA: the old connection hit EOF or an I/O error: its session was detached,<br/>kept for the retention window, its subscriptions held
    Client->>Listener: TCP connect, mutual TLS, identity from the leaf
    Client->>Listener: RegistrationRequest(the old registration_id)
    Listener->>SM: RegistrationRequest(client_id, registration_id, identity)

    alt the session is still held
        rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
        alt DESIGNED: identity differs from the session's
            SM->>SA: leave it alone
            SM-->>Listener: a new session for this identity
        end
        end
        SM->>SA: reattach to this connection, deliver what was queued
        SM-->>Listener: RegistrationResponse(Ok, the same registration_id)
    else retention over, or never existed
        SM-->>Listener: a new session (its subscriptions are gone)
    end
    Listener-->>Client: RegistrationResponse
    Client->>Client: ClientEvent::Registered, subscriptions sent again,<br/>each decided at the Listener (designed)
